Backport of php/php-src d7ddf83dde6bd0829d991a6c45aa8baa85705ff9
"Autotools: Refactor AVX-512 checks" (#14831), from PHP 8.4, without its
UPGRADING.INTERNALS note.

PHP 8.3's configure probes AVX-512 support without a cache variable, so the
php_cv_have_avx512=no and php_cv_have_avx512vbmi=no that StaticPHP passes do not
reach it. When the compiler accepts the probe's -mavx512* flags, the base64
AVX-512 kernels are compiled, and zig's clang rejects them for a baseline
x86_64 target, since their target attribute lacks evex512. With the upstream
cache checks, 8.3 leaves those kernels out exactly as PHP 8.4 and later do.

